    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside tandem in the outfield, with **Corbin Carroll** (75.69) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.14) providing our elite-tier offensive engine. **Corbin Carroll** is our primary target today, benefiting from a +4% bump due to the slow delivery of Kevin Gausman, which drastically enhances his stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our strategy. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** draws a fantastic matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.27 xERA), where his placement in the #2 hole and positive park factors push him well into the \"Strong\" start tier. We are also banking on **Henry Bolte** (61.01) to utilize his speed in the lead-off spot against Zebby Matthews, as his +10% order bonus makes him a high-efficiency play despite the platoon disadvantage.\n\nWe faced a difficult choice regarding the final utility spots, ultimately favoring **Max Muncy** (59.65) and **Mickey Moniak** (57.78) over the rest of the bench. **Max Muncy** earns his spot thanks to a park factor boost and the aforementioned theft potential against Zebby Matthews, while **Mickey Moniak** projects well because of a massive +14% platoon edge against Cade Cavalli. The most difficult bench decision was opting against **Griffin Conine** (35.44); while his underlying xwOBA remains high, the combination of facing a quality arm in Ranger Suarez and a drop to the bottom of the order rendered him too risky compared to our starters. We must remain vigilant, as **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Zach McKinstry**, and the rest remain subject to \"Lineup Pending\" fluctuations; should these starters move down in the order or be rested, we have little margin for error given the elite arms they are facing, particularly the formidable Zack Wheeler looming against **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young**.",
